4c017433e5" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315245 1145 "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $f(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & =-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=1$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=1,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315247 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315248 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315249 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315250 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315251 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1041 "selection" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315247 13194139534856 true] [17592186315246 1110 #uuid "102423a6-0915-59f1-960d-74a13e7355f4" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315247 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534856 true] [17592186315247 1111 #uuid "ad263216-6e6c-5e01-9847-17b6cf57e649" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315248 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534856 true] [17592186315248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534856 true] [17592186315248